            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Kipowi 0.8.3</h2>
<ul>
<li>Choose the sample rate when exporting audio: leave it at the source's, or convert to 44.1 or 48 kHz. Converting keeps the pitch and the length — only the number of samples per second changes.</li>
<li>Export in mono, stereo, or whatever the source is. Mono sums both sides rather than dropping one, so nothing panned hard to one side is lost.</li>
<li>The export summary says when the rate or the channels differ from the source, the way everything else that changes the file does.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
